														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4822319">
									

<p>Hey there Choysis, I'll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am neither a particularly experienced nor an offical reviewer, so take what I say with a grain of salt. With that being said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>So it's a celestial guardian of Earth (or rather, humanity) that lives in its own dimension, and the twist is that it's an axolotl? I'll be honest, I don't really like this idea, and as a general rule I'd advise staying away from supreme cosmic beings that defend Earth, as they're viewed as cliche by popular opinion on this Site. The axolotl part also just feels random and janky, and doesn't really fit in with the whole 'cosmic guardian' idea. In short, I think this idea is a cliche 'cosmic guardian entity', but the only flavour being that it's an axolotl for some reason (which feels random and forced).</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<p>Unfortunately, your narrative isn't very impressive either, just basically a highlight reel of how the axolotl has been spotted throughout history and either stopped entities capable of K-Class scenarios<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-526711-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-526711-1')">1</a></sup>, or accidentally caused collateral damage, with minimum damage to humans. The part about the paintings and carvings makes sense however, nice catch there.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>Is this idea fun or funny? I'd have to say no. It just feels kind of inane and random, assigning the role of almighty cosmic guardian to an axolotl.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As a general rule, one should stay away from almighty, nigh-omnipotent beings as SCPs (very few articles get away with this. Actually, I think there's <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-343">only one</a> that does), especially ones that only exist to protect humanity from other SCPs. It just seems cliche, and, with the axolotl part, kind of random and silly.</p>
<p>I'd recommend three things:<br />
1. Consider overhauling your idea (maybe making it a bit less OP and/or random) and/or story<br />
2. Check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for great advice on ideation, story writing, and more!<br />
3. Contact reviewers from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> for alternative opinions from experienced reviewers</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your idea in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-526711-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-526711-2')">2</a></sup>:<br />
A cosmic, all-powerful axolotl that lives in its own dimension, emerging only to engage with and stop entities causing K-Class events.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-526711-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-526711-1')">1</a>. Being nitpicky here, but there is <em>no way</em> the Foundation names an anomaly, especially one capable of causing K-Class events, &quot;Lil' Devil&quot;. This serves to break the suspension of disbelief of readers, something that articles should try their best to maintain (this is, although fictional, a <em>scientific</em> organisation after all).</div>
