					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4874276&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605791351" alt="TheAlienBaby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4874276)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;" >TheAlienBaby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605784108 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Nov 2020 11:08</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13867162/monster-maker">Monster maker</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4822298">
									

<p>Hey there Researcher Penguin, I'll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am neither a particularly experienced nor official reviewer, so take everything I say with a grain of salt. With that said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>Ok, so your concept is an amusement park run by a British businessman with a bunch of anomalous creatures of all shapes and sizes contained in habitats for viewing, however, it's all a lure to bring people in to turn them into more anomalous creatures. Unfortunately, I can't say I'm very keen on this idea, as it isn't very original (just a parade of random monsters displayed for people to see) or interesting (see previous point) and lacks substance (i.e a good story).</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> none</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yikes. Narrative is almost a necessity for <em>every</em> article nowadays (Series VI), and it's come to be expected that all the newer articles have something at least resembling a story (and if not, an extremely strong premise, which this isn't). Without story, your idea just&#8230; falls flat on its face. There isn't anything interesting here, just a weird monster amusement park to be locked away and never seen again. This may have been acceptable in Series I, but not anymore. I'd suggest brainstorming a story before you continue with ideation, as this is one of the most vital parts of not only yours but any SCP.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>You have an okay hook (anomalous businessmen with <em>many</em> anomalous creatures at their back), but as I stated previously, your idea collapses without a story to back it up. Work on the story first.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Hate to sound like a broken record, but story is what you need here. If you're planning on continuing this idea, then work on the story, the backbone of your article, first. Think of a genre (horror, dramatic, mystery, etc.), think of what you want your readers to feel, then try and build a narrative off of that<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-711582-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-711582-1')">1</a></sup>.</p>
<p>I'll recommend two more things while I'm here:<br />
1. Check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for some great tips and essays on everything, from building stories to pacing articles and more!<br />
2. Reach out to reviewers on the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> for some alternative opinions and advice from experienced reviewers!</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your idea in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-711582-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-711582-2')">2</a></sup>:<br />
An amusement park full of wildly varying anomalous creatures, run by an anomalous businessmen who uses it to lure humans in and turn them into more anomalous creatures.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-711582-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-711582-1')">1</a>. I know this is vague, but creative ideation is an esoteric business that differs for everyone, and this works for me.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-711582-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-711582-2')">2</a>. This is to give you an idea of the bare bones of what a reviewer sees from your concept, thereby giving you the opportunity to change it accordingly.</div>
</div>

