<p>The idea is for an SCP that is a roadside motel in the Arizona desert. This motel is a fixed point in multiple realities. The different worlds can be viewed from the different room's windows. The inside is infinitely bigger inside than outside, and labyrinthine. Examples include a barren white world of perpetual night, at the bottom of an alien ocean, an alien swamp, and etc. Creatures and other entities can break through the windows from time to time. There appears to be no staff, until those who are drawn to enter it &quot;check out&quot; the next day. The staffs' features can never be remembered by those that observe them. It is Euclid class, and fenced off with posted guards. Yet, still, sometimes civilians and even a guard or two, somehow, manage to enter.</p>

							</div>

								
					
