<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> There is an amusement park containing various creatures led by a British businessman, the monsters very wildly ranging from literal planet consuming monsters to sentient bug-like creatures all contained and safe for viewing, it being encouraged to observe them in their &quot;habitats&quot;. The habitats are unusually fitted for the creature at hand with the supplies for upkeep never seen. The British businessman himself is the only one there seemingly doing everything there being everywhere in the park. The monsters at the park however were once humans. When the Businessman gets bored of the current attractions he lures people selecting three interesting individuals and giving them free items. These items slowly transform the person into one a monster before being brought in by him to display.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> none</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> It presents the foundation with a large amount of anomalous creatures all relatively safe with the main concern being its owner and manager the buisnessman</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I haven't yet decided if the man will have a known identity. I'm still pondering if what to keep mystified about the man and his attractions. suggestions are very welcome.</p>

